"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"When you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, sulfur.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder within the Archipelago Launcher directory. BepInEx will then be downloaded into the SULFUR game directory, along with the Archipelago folder and its Native UI Lib dependency mod, which will be placed in BepInEx\\plugins.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"SULFUR is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file. When 'sulfur.apworld' is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once everything is set up, go to the 'Options' and there you should be able to see an Archipelago button.\n\nIn the 'Hostname' field, enter 'archipelago.gg'.\n\nIn the 'Port' field, enter the port. This is a 5-digit number that you can find on the website after creating a new room.\n\nIn 'Slot', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nThe 'Password' field is optional. If the host did not set one, leave it blank.\n\nFinally, you can start a new run and you should be connected!",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"You have 2 revert options, both can't be enabled at the same time.\n\nIf you use the 'Clear AP Mods' option it will only delete the mods that are required for SULFUR Archipelago.\n\nIf you use the 'Full Clear BepInEx' option it will delete everything related to BepInEx and mods. If other mods are detected an additionnal confirmation will appear.",
